From d6c8805a9597ed00596848ba099bf70c35fcc325 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:01:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Settings dialog, simitone.ini, diagnostics report, hotkey
 focus guard

- SimitoneSettings (Documents/Simitone/simitone.ini): Simitone's own
  switches (shimmy, diagnostics, draw routes) and start-up options that
  used to be command line only (3D, renderer, anti-aliasing, touch UI,
  no sound, lighting, shaders, transitions). Switches are pushed into
  SimAntics VMFeatures at start and on every change.
- Options > Settings (new gear button) opens UISettingsDialog: sections
  Simulation / Camera & Controls / Sound / Display / Debug, with paging.
  It also exposes the existing FreeSO settings Simitone uses (volumes,
  edge scroll, fullscreen, frame rate, language). Changes save at once;
  ones that need a restart are marked and the dialog says so.
- Program.cs reads the start-up options from simitone.ini; command line
  switches still win. The user folder is now set before GlobalSettings
  is first read, so -lang/-hz no longer put config.ini next to the exe.
- Diagnostics report: write_routes cheat or Settings > Debug writes
  Documents/Simitone/diagnostics/diagnostics-<time>.txt. The cheat box
  toggles (shimmy, draw_routes, new: diagnostics) now change and save the
  same settings.
- Hotkeys (speed keys, Space, F1-F4, camera keys, Delete/Escape while
  holding an object) are ignored while a visible text field has focus;
  the cheat box releases focus when hidden. Space no longer throws on a
  lot without a family.
- Tests: ring buffer test; the runner runs several suites.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
